# Step 5 - Offers (branch step-5-offers). Acceptance file.
#
# How these results were produced (read this before trusting a PASS):
# - The requests below were NOT sent through this file in an HTTP client. Each case
#   was executed as an equivalent request by the PowerShell driver
#   (%TEMP%\opencode\s5_offers.ps1) against the running app (http://localhost:5181,
#   Development, NEBRASDB_Step1). The method, path, body and expected status are the
#   same; the driver is the evidence. Final driver run (stamp 013150354):
#   91 PASS / 0 FAIL. The parallel-approval scenario is executed separately by
#   docs/tests/scripts/parallel-approval.ps1 (final run stamp 014108617: 7 PASS / 0 FAIL).
#   The obsolete root wrapper docs/tests/parallel-approval.ps1 was archived and removed on
#   24 October 2026 and is not a supported command path.
# - Identity is taken from the JWT only (ICurrentUser). Routes/bodies carry NO actor
#   ids. Requests below therefore have no user ids in URLs or bodies.
# - Fixture ids quoted below are the ones from the last full driver run:
#   grid 5 = "S5-G10-013150354" (10 MW); lands L1=188, L1A=189, L1B=190, L2=191
#   (all Verified), LRAW=192 (Draft). Offers 13..23 are that run's offers:
#     13 = i1 on L1 (Accepted), 14 = i2 on L1 (PendingLandlordResponse, preserved), 15 = i3 on L1 (PendingAdminApproval, preserved),
#     16 = i1 on L1A (Accepted), 17 = i2 on L1B (PendingAdminApproval),
#     18/19 = i3 on L2 (WithdrawnByInvestor), 20 = i1 on L2 (WithdrawnByInvestor),
#     21 = i2 on L2 (RejectedByInvestor), 22 = i1 on L2 (RejectedByLandlord),
#     23 = i2 on L2 (RejectedByAdmin).
# - Result legend, on the line under each case title:
#   PASS     executed by the driver; the actual status matched the expectation
#   FAIL     executed; the actual status did not match (none; final run 91/0 and 7/0)
#   BLOCKED  not executed (none in Step 5).
# - Status mapping (Enums/OfferStatus.cs): 1 PendingLandlordResponse, 2
#   PendingInvestorResponse, 3 PendingAdminApproval, 4 Accepted, 5 RejectedByLandlord,
#   6 RejectedByInvestor, 7 RejectedByAdmin, 8 WithdrawnByInvestor, 9 Closed.
#
# Coverage map (task T1..T15):
#   T1  = 5.1 create gates (403/409/404/401)        T2  = 5.2 identity from token
#   T3  = 5.3 negotiation turn rules                T4  = 5.3 read authorization
#   T5  = 5.4 D-14 terminal does not block          T6  = 5.5 counter-offer versions
#   T7  = 5.6 S3 approval (competitors preserved)   T8  = 5.6 reservation + ExpiresAt
#   T9  = 5.6 S4 grid-capacity (10 MW / two 6 MW)   T10 = 5.6 no partial state on 409
#   T11 = 5.7 admin rejection                       T12 = 5.7 BR-O3 withdraw allow-list
#   T13 = 5.8 validation attributes                 T14 = 5.9 parallel approval
#   T15 = removal of public close endpoint + GET my / land / pending-admin-approval

