### ============ T6 / 5.5 counter-offer versioning (one transaction) ============

# Versions for offer 13 (created + landlord counter + investor counter):
#   SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(CASE WHEN IS_CURRENT=1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), MAX(VERSION_NUMBER)
#   FROM OFFER_VERSIONS WHERE OFFER_ID = 13;
# Result: PASS (3 | 1 | 3; driver S5-29) - exactly one IsCurrent=1 row and versions 1..3.
# The current version row is version 3, and OFFERS.ACCEPTED_VERSION_ID points at it
# (S5-29b), so a signed/accepted offer always references the exact agreed version.
#
# Previous-version deactivation and the new-version insert happen inside ONE database
# transaction: the deactivation is saved with its own SaveChanges BEFORE the insert
# (required by the filtered unique index UX_OFFER_VERSIONS_CURRENT_OFFER from Step 1),
# and a DbUpdateException on that index is mapped to 409.

